  "content": {
    "text": "96\n\n The Contract Clause That Could Outlive Your Deal\nHi Sara,\nLet\u2019s talk about a contract term that\u2019s as exciting as it sounds- in fact, this is one of the only contract terms with a name that sounds more like it belongs in a dystopian thriller than a 40 page purchase agreement: Survival.\nSounds intense, right? That\u2019s because it kind of is.\nAnd let me tell you\u2014if you\u2019re negotiating a purchase agreement and glossing over the survival clause, you\u2019re making a rookie mistake.\nWhat is \u201cSurvival\u201d?\nNo, it\u2019s not a Hunger Games reference. In a contract, \u201csurvival\u201d refers to how long your reps and warranties live on after closing.\nHere\u2019s why it matters:\nIf the agreement says nothing about survival? Those reps may hang around indefinitely (or until your local statute of limitations gives them the boot).\nThat\u2019s great for the buyer, not so great for the seller.\nThe Seller\u2019s Dilemma:\nIf you're the seller, you don\u2019t want to be on the hook forever. You want a survival period that caps your liability\u201412, 18, maybe 24 months.\nThe Buyer\u2019s Balancing Act:\nFrom the buyer\u2019s perspective, you need some amount of time. You maybe won\u2019t uncover shady vendor arrangements, ghost clients, or mysteriously disappearing revenue until you\u2019ve gone through at least one full operating cycle. That\u2019s why most buyers push for 18+ months\u2014to uncover issues and have time to act on them.\nPro Tip: If your contract says nothing about survival and you're the seller\u2014fix that. Immediately.\nIf it says nothing and you're the buyer\u2014enjoy the gift that keeps on giving\u2013at least through the applicable statute of limitations.\nSurvival may sound like a footnote, but it\u2019s actually a battleground in disguise. And if you want to fight smart, you better understand what you\u2019re agreeing to.\nCurious how to navigate these terms like a pro? \nCheck out my courses over at DealAcademy.org and subscribe for more legal low-downs that actually make sense.\nTo smarter deals and fewer regrets,\nSara Sharp\nPartner, SK&S Law Group\nFounder, Deal Academy\n\n For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our Dealmakers Youtube Channel where you'll find Sara's Weekly Wine Down, where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&A Experts and Dealmakers.\nYou can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.\n\n Copyright \u00a9 2025\u00a0 Someday Consultants, All rights reserved. \n\n Our e-mail address is:\ninfo@dealacademy.org\n\n Want to change how you receive these emails?\n You can unsubscribe from this list.",
