->\n            \n      <div class=\"mj-column-per-100 mj-outlook-group-fix\" style=\"font-size:0px;text-align:left;direction:ltr;display:inline-block;vertical-align:top;width:100%;\">\n        \n      <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"100%\">\n        <tbody>\n          <tr>\n            <td style=\"vertical-align:top;padding-top:0px;padding-right:0px;padding-bottom:0px;padding-left:0px;\">\n              \n    <table border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" role=\"presentation\" style=\"\" width=\"100%\">\n          <tbody>\n            \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"center\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:10px;padding-right:20px;padding-bottom:10px;padding-left:20px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <p style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:100%;\">\n      </p>\n      \n      <!--[if mso | IE]><table align=\"center\" border=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" style=\"border-top:solid 2px rgba(242, 247, 250, 1);font-size:1px;margin:0px auto;width:520px;\" role=\"presentation\" width=\"520px\" ><tr><td style=\"height:0;line-height:0;\"> &nbsp;\n</td></tr></table><![endif]-->\n    \n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <div style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;color:#000000;\"><h2 style=\"margin-top: 14pt;margin-bottom: 4pt;\"><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">The Contract Clause That Could Outlive Your Deal</span></h2><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">Hi Sara,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Let\u2019s talk about a contract term that\u2019s as exciting as it sounds- in fact, this is one of the only contract terms with a name that sounds more like it belongs in a dystopian thriller than a 40 page purchase agreement: Survival.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Sounds intense, right? That\u2019s because it kind of is.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">And let me tell you\u2014if you\u2019re negotiating a purchase agreement and glossing over the survival clause, you\u2019re making a rookie mistake.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><strong>What is \u201cSurvival\u201d?</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">No, it\u2019s not a Hunger Games reference. In a contract, \u201csurvival\u201d refers to how long your reps and warranties live on after closing.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Here\u2019s why it matters:</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">If the agreement says nothing about survival? Those reps may hang around indefinitely (or until your local statute of limitations gives them the boot).</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">That\u2019s great for the buyer, not so great for the seller.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><strong>The Seller\u2019s Dilemma:</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">If you're the seller, you don\u2019t want to be on the hook forever. You want a survival period that caps your liability\u201412, 18, maybe 24 months.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\"><strong>The Buyer\u2019s Balancing Act:</strong></span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">From the buyer\u2019s perspective, you need some amount of time. You maybe won\u2019t uncover shady vendor arrangements, ghost clients, or mysteriously disappearing revenue until you\u2019ve gone through at least one full operating cycle. That\u2019s why most buyers push for 18+ months\u2014to uncover issues and have time to act on them.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Pro Tip: If your contract says nothing about survival and you're the seller\u2014fix that. Immediately.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">If it says nothing and you're the buyer\u2014enjoy the gift that keeps on giving\u2013at least through the applicable statute of limitations.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Survival may sound like a footnote, but it\u2019s actually a battleground in disguise. And if you want to fight smart, you better understand what you\u2019re agreeing to.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Curious how to navigate these terms like a pro? </span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Check out my courses over at </span><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/d2670209488?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: #3425db !important; color: #3425db !important; font-size: 14px\">DealAcademy.org</span></a><span style=\"color: #3425db !important; color: #3425db !important; font-size: 14px\"> </span><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">and subscribe for more legal low-downs that actually make sense.</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">To smarter deals and fewer regrets,</span></p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Sara Sharp</span><br><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Partner, SK&amp;S Law Group</span><br><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0); color: rgb(0, 0, 0); font-size: 14px\">Founder, Deal Academy</span></p></div>\n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <td align=\"left\" style=\"font-size:0px;padding:10px 25px;padding-top:12px;padding-right:24px;padding-bottom:12px;padding-left:24px;word-break:break-word;\">\n                      \n      <div style=\"font-family:arial, helvetica, sans-serif;font-size:14px;line-height:1.25;text-align:left;color:#000000;\"><p>For more helpful lessons from Deal Academy, check out our <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/9f2056fbc88?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn\"><span style=\"color: rgb(52, 37, 219); color: rgb(52, 37, 219)\">Dealmakers Youtube Channel </span></a>where you'll find Sara's <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://link.msgsndr.com/email-tracking/5116926bb4f?contactId=xoXEjJhxZU4nfwkScSXn&amp;v=csIoWCXhXsE&amp;t=15s\" title=\"Weekly Wine Down\"><span style=\"color: rgb(52, 37, 219); font-size: 14px; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; color: rgb(52, 37, 219)\">Weekly Wine Down,</span></a> where she talks about what she's seen in the industry this week and interviews with M&amp;A Experts and Dealmakers.</p><p>You can check out some recent Dealmakers YouTube videos by clicking the images below.</p></div>\n    \n                    </td>\n                  </tr>\n                    \n                    \n                      \n                    <tr>\n                    <t